---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
---
<Base title={"IFS Therapy in Utah County | Tangible Therapy"} description={"Discover IFS therapy in Utah County at Tangible Mental Health. Heal and harmonize your inner self with expert support. Book a free consultation today!"}>
<section class="sec t-black h-medium has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:40;--mrows:16">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/7/24/21;--m:1/2/11/10"><div class="rte"><div class="scaled"><span class="scaled-in"><h1 class="ta-center">&nbsp; IFS&nbsp;&nbsp;</h1></span></div><h2 class="ta-center">Internal Family Systems&nbsp; &nbsp;</h2><p class="ta-center">Internal Family Systems (IFS) is a therapeutic approach that views the mind as an inner family composed of distinct parts, each with its own unique characteristics, emotions, and roles. IFS posits that these parts interact with one another, often mirroring the dynamics of an external family. The central idea is that every person has a core Self, which is a source of wisdom, compassion, and calmness. When the Self is in a leadership position, it can harmonize and heal the various parts, leading to greater psychological well-being. This approach emphasizes understanding and appreciating each part, including those that may carry pain or exhibit extreme behaviors, as they all contribute to the individual's internal system.</p><p>The therapeutic process in IFS involves identifying and getting to know these parts, particularly the wounded Exiles that carry the burdens of past traumas and the protective Managers and Firefighters that try to shield the individual from pain. By fostering a trusting relationship between the Self and these parts, individuals can help their parts release extreme roles and heal. This often leads to profound shifts in self-perception and behavior, as the previously conflicting parts begin to work together harmoniously. IFS is praised for its non-pathologizing stance and its empowering belief in the person's inherent capacity for self-healing and transformation.</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:25/4/41/24;--m:11/2/17/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><figure class="img fill"><img src="/images/infographic-on-internal-81ac3d.jpg" alt="Infographic on Internal Family Systems Therapy with bubbles containing text around a central title." width="2158" height="1272" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
</div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#fff" /></section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-in" style="padding-top:6.6vmax;padding-bottom:6.6vmax">
<div class="wrap"><div class="list-title rte"><p>What you’ll get</p></div><ul class="ulist ulist-simple circle" style="--per:3;--tfs:calc((2.6 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--bfs:calc((0.9 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--cw:75%;--mw:75%"><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="#" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Fifty minutes of professional insight and unconditional support</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>A better relationship with yourself, your thoughts and your emotions.</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Clinically precise guidance tailored to you and the problems you’re facing.</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>New skills guided by expertise and experience that will create meaningful change.</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>A comfortable and inviting atmosphere that promotes mindful reflection and calm.</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="/" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>New insights into how your mind works and why it engages in unhelpful patterns.</p></div></div></li></ul></div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#acb9ac" /></section>

<section class="sec t-black h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/4/26;--m:1/2/4/10"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">✺ Frequently asked questions ✺</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/2/14/13;--m:5/2/13/10"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>Am I covered by insurance?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Currently our practice works with, United Healthcare, Blue Cross Blue Shield, Regence, EMI, DMBA, PEHP, &amp; Select Health. This is a covered service under all major insurances, however we recommend that you reach out to your insurance company to understand specific copay/deductible amounts.</p></div></details><details><summary>What is the cost without insurance?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Our cash pay rate is $150 per session. </p></div></details><details><summary>How is Tangible different from other therapy practices?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Tangible is built on the core philosophy of offering skills-based therapy. Our therapists are dedicated to equipping you with practical skills that not only facilitate your healing process but also enable you to sustain your wellbeing long after therapy has ended.</p></div></details></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/15/14/26;--m:13/2/21/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>How do I know if my therapist is a good fit?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Ensuring that you are compatible with your therapist is a critical part of the therapeutic process. We are happy to offer a 15-minute free consultation call with any therapist to determine if they are the right one for you.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do you work with ecclesiastical leaders (Bishops)?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Yes, we are more than happy to coordinate care. Please let us know when scheduling an appointment and we will take care of the rest.</p></div></details><details><summary>How long will it take?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Duration of care can depend on a wide variety of factors. However, most people see significant progress in 8-12 weeks. </p></div></details></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</Base>
